  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 311 AM MST TUE NOV 17 2026\nAs the upper trough continues steering out east across our area on \nFriday, valley rain and mountain snow will continue in the morning. \nWith snow levels expected to briefly drop to valley floors in the \nearly hours, valleys may see a rain/snow mix Friday morning. \nPrecipitation will completely taper off by late Friday/early \nSaturday as the system moves out of our area. A brief ridge will \nbuild into the area early Saturday, returning a short dry break \nbefore another Pacific upper trough digs into the northwest region \nlate Saturday. The area will see slight to moderate chances of \nprecipitation late Saturday through early Sunday. But come late \nSunday, there is considerable guidance uncertainty over how \nmuch precipitation the area will receive as the trough digs down\ninto California and the Great Basin. For now, higher terrain \nareas will see the higher chances of precipitation late Sunday \nthrough early Tuesday. Temperatures will hover near or slightly \nbelow normal throughout the long term period.",
